{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi James, sorry about the rough morning. I checked both issues. Your desktop (BL-DT-0108) is showing as offline, and the floor 2 printer (BL-PR-FL2) is also offline for everyone, so this looks like a problem on the floor rather than with your account. Your account is active, and your recent sign-ins look normal. I've passed both issues to our second-line team with the details. While you wait, could you check that the network cable is firmly plugged into your desktop and that the printer's power and network cable are connected? If the printer has an error on its screen, please let us know what it says. If you need to print before it's fixed, you can use another printer on the floor and we'll help you add it if needed.",
  "internal_note": "Sender user_id 8, James O'Connor, Warehouse Supervisor, Operations, America/Chicago, usual hours 06:00-14:00. Account active, not sign-in blocked, no failed logins, VPN enabled. Triage said user_blocked: true, but the lookup shows sign_in_blocked: false, so the triage flag looks wrong. Desktop BL-DT-0108 (Win 11, assigned to sender): online false, last check-in 2026-10-11 01:15 UTC, no warnings, disk 78% free. Printer BL-PR-FL2: online false, last check-in 2026-10-10 22:15 UTC, no warnings, offline for all users per KB-022, so the printer is the problem, not the laptop. Sign-ins last 14 days: all successful, corporate and residential networks, no MFA denials, nothing unusual. Last corporate sign-in was 2026-10-09. Two floor 2 devices offline with no warnings may point to a shared switch or network segment outage, so please check the floor 2 network first. KB-022 power cycle and cable checks are not yet done on site. No KB article covers a wired desktop losing network (KB-014 is Wi-Fi only). Escalating for network investigation of BL-DT-0108 and the floor 2 printer.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-022",
    "KB-014"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
